collections:
  - folderType: environment
    name: Swagger Petstore
    documentation: |-
      # Swagger Petstore

      This is a sample server Petstore server.  You can find out more about Swagger at [http://swagger.io](http://swagger.io) or on [irc.freenode.net, #swagger](http://swagger.io/irc/).  For this sample, you can use the api key &#x60;special-key&#x60; to test the authorization filters.

      **Version:** 1.0.7

      **Terms of Service:** [http://swagger.io/terms/](http://swagger.io/terms/)

      ## Contact

      - **Email:** [apiteam@swagger.io](mailto:apiteam@swagger.io)

      ## License

      [Apache 2.0](http://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0.html)

      ## External Documentation

      [Find out more about Swagger](http://swagger.io)

      **Host:** `localhost:8080`

      **Base Path:** `/api`

      **Schemes:** `https`, `http`

      ## Models

      ```mermaid
      classDiagram
        class Category {
          - id? : integer
          - name? : string
        }
        class Pet {
          - id? : integer
          - category? : Category
          + name : string
          + photoUrls : array<string>
          - tags? : array<Tag>
          - status? : string
        }
        class Tag {
          - id? : integer
          - name? : string
        }
        class ApiResponse {
          - code? : integer
          - type? : string
          - message? : string
        }
        class Order {
          - id? : integer
          - petId? : integer
          - quantity? : integer
          - shipDate? : string
          - status? : string
          - complete? : boolean
        }
        class User {
          - id? : integer
          - username? : string
          - firstName? : string
          - lastName? : string
          - email? : string
          - password? : string
          - phone? : string
          - userStatus? : integer
        }
        Pet --> Category
        Pet --> Tag
      ```
    tags: []
    configuration: {}
    environments:
      - name: Default
        variables:
          - key: port
            value:
              type: string
              value: '8080'
            description: ''
          - key: scheme
            value:
              type: string
              value: http
            description: ''
          - key: domain
            value:
              type: string
              value: localhost
            description: ''
          - key: baseUrl
            value:
              type: string
              value: '{{scheme}}://{{domain}}:{{port}}'
            description: ''
        subEnvironments:
          - name: Production
            variables:
              - key: scheme
                value:
                  type: string
                  value: https
                description: ''
              - key: domain
                value:
                  type: string
                  value: petstore.com
                description: ''
              - key: baseUrl
                value:
                  type: string
                  value: '{{scheme}}://{{domain}}:{{port}}'
                description: ''
    items:
      - name: pet
        documentation: "# pet\r\n\r\nEverything about your Pets\r\n\r\n## External Documentation\r\n\r\n[Find out more](http://swagger.io)"
        tags:
          - pet
        configuration: {}
        items:
          - type: http
            name: Find pet by ID
            documentation: |-
              # Find pet by ID

              Returns a single pet

              **Operation ID:** `getPetById`

              ## Produces

              - `application/json`
              - `application/xml`

              ## Parameters

              | Name | Location | Type | Required | Description |
              |------|----------|------|----------|-------------|
              | `petId` | path | integer (int64) | Yes | ID of pet to return |

              ## Types

              ### Pet

              **Reference:** `#/definitions/Pet`

              ```mermaid
              classDiagram
                class Pet {
                  - id? : integer
                  - category? : Category
                  + name : string
                  + photoUrls : array<string>
                  - tags? : array<Tag>
                  - status? : string
                }
              ```


              | Property | Type | Required | Description |
              |----------|------|----------|-------------|
              | `id` | integer | No |  |
              | `category` | Category | No |  |
              | `name` | string | Yes |  |
              | `photoUrls` | array&lt;string&gt; | Yes |  |
              | `tags` | array&lt;Tag&gt; | No |  |
              | `status` | string | No | pet status in the store |


              ## Responses

              ### 200
              successful operation

              **Schema:** `#/definitions/Pet`


              ### 400
              Invalid ID supplied



              ### 404
              Pet not found



              ## Security

              - **api_key**
            tags:
              - pet
            method: GET
            url: '{{baseUrl}}/api/pet/{{petId}}'
            headers: []
            params: []
            pathParams:
              - key: petId
                value:
                  type: string
                  value: ''
                description: ID of pet to return
          - type: http
            name: Add a new pet to the store
            documentation: |-
              # Add a new pet to the store

              **Operation ID:** `addPet`

              ## Consumes

              - `application/json`
              - `application/xml`

              ## Produces

              - `application/json`
              - `application/xml`

              ## Parameters

              | Name | Location | Type | Required | Description |
              |------|----------|------|----------|-------------|
              | `body` | body | #/definitions/Pet | Yes | Pet object that needs to be added to the store |

              ## Types

              ### Pet

              **Reference:** `#/definitions/Pet`

              ```mermaid
              classDiagram
                class Pet {
                  - id? : integer
                  - category? : Category
                  + name : string
                  + photoUrls : array<string>
                  - tags? : array<Tag>
                  - status? : string
                }
              ```


              | Property | Type | Required | Description |
              |----------|------|----------|-------------|
              | `id` | integer | No |  |
              | `category` | Category | No |  |
              | `name` | string | Yes |  |
              | `photoUrls` | array&lt;string&gt; | Yes |  |
              | `tags` | array&lt;Tag&gt; | No |  |
              | `status` | string | No | pet status in the store |


              ## Responses

              ### 405
              Invalid input



              ## Security

              - **petstore_auth**: `write:pets`, `read:pets`
            tags:
              - pet
            method: POST
            url: '{{baseUrl}}/api/pet'
            headers: []
            params: []
            pathParams: []
            body:
              type: text
              content: |-
                {
                  "id": 0,
                  "category": {
                    "id": 0,
                    "name": ""
                  },
                  "name": "",
                  "photoUrls": [
                    ""
                  ],
                  "tags": [
                    {
                      "id": 0,
                      "name": ""
                    }
                  ],
                  "status": "available"
                }
